      "title": "Applying the Vector Form of the Chain Rule to a Function of Three Variables"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f80a65f1-228c-56d7-bd21-0adf634a97c7",
      ":question/problem": "If $f(x,y,z)=- 2 x - 2 y + 3 z$ and $\\mathbf{r}(t)=(t)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(t^{2})\\,\\mathbf{j}+(t^{2})\\,\\mathbf{k},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))].$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "e3a36bd7-3662-5bd4-8dda-2ca3463369ab",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "fe89e045-e71e-58cc-8b5a-2d3a695d0759",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "2 \\left(3 t - 1\\right)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "33dcffd6-d890-531c-a70d-35f01e18824a",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "t \\left(t - 2\\right)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "3e62ee1e-c1cf-5836-ae82-3f26f7ead143",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "2 \\left(t - 1\\right)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "70133580-4054-5942-ad41-3e90ad2a9852",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "- 2 \\left(2 t + 1\\right)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "67f30ea1-b3b7-53c5-8cf4-a3b06bae8a9d",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "2 t"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "3e62ee1e-c1cf-5836-ae82-3f26f7ead143"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]=∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 2 x - 2 y + 3 z)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 2 x - 2 y + 3 z)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(- 2 x - 2 y + 3 z)\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =(-2)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(-2)\\,\\mathbf{j}+(3)\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t,y=t^{2},$ and $z=t^{2}$ into the above to find $∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =(-2)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(-2)\\,\\mathbf{j}+(3)\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $\\mathbf{r}(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =(1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(2 t)\\,\\mathbf{j}+(2 t)\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))] & =∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((-2)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(-2)\\,\\mathbf{j}+(3)\\,\\mathbf{k})\\cdot ((1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(2 t)\\,\\mathbf{j}+(2 t)\\,\\mathbf{k}) \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (1)+(-2)\\cdot (2 t)+(3)\\cdot (2 t) \\\\  & =(-2)+(- 4 t)+(6 t) \\\\  & =2 \\left(t - 1\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
